        "original_id": "c41858a0-7e41-5ba8-905d-6bffc1b715dd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Reed, Johnny Bright, Mike Pringle, Ron Lancaster\n- Organizations: Canadian Football League, Saskatchewan Roughriders, Drake University\n- Events: 54th Grey Cup, 1966 Grey Cup championship\n- Topics: CFL history, running backs, college football\n\nFacts:\n- Johnny Bright was born on June 11, 1930, and he later played college football at Drake University.\n- Johnny Bright was a professional Canadian football player in the Canadian Football League, and he died on December 14, 1983.\n- In 1966, Ron Lancaster led the Saskatchewan Roughriders to the franchise's first Grey Cup championship as the team's starting quarterback.\n- Ron Lancaster was the starting quarterback for the Saskatchewan Roughriders for 16 seasons and is the franchise's all-time leader in passing yards, attempts, completions, touchdowns, and interceptions.\n- In the 54th Grey Cup, George Reed was the MVP with 31 rushes for 133 yards and one rushing touchdown.\n- George Reed, along with Mike Pringle and Johnny Bright, is one of the players most often mentioned as the greatest running back in Canadian Football League history.",
